% The white SNFG symbol for each saccharide residue with no SNFG symbol of its own (#279).
%
% SNFG: a monosaccharide absent from its Table 1 is drawn as a white symbol with a letter, in the
% white symbol of its generic type where one fits - a circle for a hexose, a triangle for a
% deoxyhexose - and otherwise in the white pentagon. Which type fits is decided here, residue by
% residue, because the dictionaries' superclasses do not say it reliably: Rho, a 2,3,6-trideoxy sugar,
% is filed under Hexose, and Ole, Cym and The under Unknown.
%
% Columns, tab-separated: the residue's name; the residue_styles_snfg row whose white symbol it is
% drawn in (Hex, HexA, dHex, ddHex, Pen, ddNon, Unknown, or Assigned for the pentagon); why.
%
% Every saccharide residue with no SNFG row of its own is listed, so that each is a decision made and
% not a default; the tests hold this file to that.
